The agent understands the user's context and dynamically uses knowledge and tools.

They connect the chatbot to a website.

They connect the same chatbot to WhatsApp and Telegram.

They publish the chatbot.

They monitor all conversations, response quality, integrations, latency, and AI costs from one dashboard.

The same chatbot intelligence must work consistently across channels.

A non-technical user should be able to perform the basic setup without writing code.

A developer should be able to extend the platform using the SDK and optional Python integrations.

The system must be designed as a commercial multi-tenant SaaS, not an internal single-company chatbot.

## FINAL PRINCIPLE

The most important feature of KRESNA is not the chatbot builder, the number of integrations, or the dashboard.

It is the intelligence of the actual conversation.

A user should be able to talk naturally, explain a problem in their own words, change topics, provide incomplete information, and ask for actions without learning a predefined chatbot workflow.

The AI must understand the situation, retrieve relevant knowledge, choose appropriate actions, and continue until it can resolve the request or transparently explain its limitation.

BUILD A PRODUCT THAT MAKES CREATING A CHATBOT EASY AND USING A CHATBOT FEEL NATURAL.

START WITH PHASE 0.

After presenting the research and architecture, proceed with Phase 1 only. Implement real working functionality, not static mockups. Maintain a clear project roadmap and test report.

Do not claim that the entire product is complete until all acceptance criteria have been verified.